<section class="section" id="start">
  <h2>Get started</h2>
  <div class="prose">
    <p>With Docker:</p>
    <pre class="code"><code>git clone {{ site.repo }}.git
cd llm-router
docker compose up --wait     # http://localhost:3000, config in ./data</code></pre>

    <p>Or from source, with Node 22 or newer:</p>
    <pre class="code"><code>npm install
npm run dev                  # UI on http://localhost:3000</code></pre>

    <p>
      On first run the server generates a bearer token and prints it once;
      paste it into the UI when asked. Set <code>LLM_ROUTER_TOKEN</code> to
      choose it yourself, or <code>SECURE_LOCAL_NET=true</code> to run without
      one on a network you trust. Then:
    </p>
    <ol>
      <li>
        <strong>Providers → Add provider.</strong> A name
        (<code>ollama</code>), the base URL including the version path
        (<code>http://localhost:11434/v1</code>) and, if it needs one, an API
        key.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Workspaces → New workspace.</strong> Switch on the providers it
        should serve.
      </li>
      <li>Copy the connection details from the workspace page.</li>
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section" id="connect">
  <h2>Connect a client</h2>
  <div class="prose">
    <table>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row">Base URL</th>
          <td>
            <code>http://&lt;host&gt;:3000/w/&lt;slug&gt;/v1</code> for a
            workspace, <code>http://&lt;host&gt;:3000/v1</code> for every
            enabled provider
          </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row">API key</th>
          <td>the router's token</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row">Model</th>
          <td><code>&lt;provider&gt;/&lt;model&gt;</code>, such as <code>ollama/qwen3:32b</code></td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <pre class="code"><code>curl http://localhost:3000/w/research/v1/chat/completions \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $LLM_ROUTER_TOKEN" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"model": "ollama/qwen3:32b", "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "Hello"}]}'</code></pre>

    <pre class="code"><code>from openai import OpenAI

client = OpenAI(base_url="http://localhost:3000/w/research/v1", api_key="&lt;router token&gt;")
client.chat.completions.create(model="ollama/qwen3:32b", messages=[{"role": "user", "content": "Hello"}])</code></pre>
  </div>

  <p class="readme-link">
    Endpoints, configuration and the design decisions are in the project README:
    <a href="{{ site.repo }}#readme" rel="noopener">{{ site.repo }}</a>
  </p>
</section>
